# Project Index

The optional `INDEX.md` beside this skill maps modules to paths and responsibilities. It is a navigation aid; the actual files are authoritative.

## Locate

Use a relevant index entry when useful, or search the project directly. Read `details/<module>.md` only for the module involved. Reuse information already established in the conversation. A missing or stale index does not block an answer or require a whole-project scan.

## Maintain

Update the index when requested or when the task reorganizes major modules and the project already maintains this map. Initialize it only as part of a requested structural overview or index task. Skip `.git`, dependencies and generated output.

Keep a short table of module, path, responsibility and optional detail link. Move substantial module-specific context into `details/`. Verify changed paths exist and record the update date. Small bug fixes do not trigger index maintenance.

## Completion

A lookup answers the user's location question with verified paths. An update produces an accurate map of the requested scope, without copying business code into the index.
